WEBVTT

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.720
-[man] Captain Daly.
-Report.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.120
A non-federation vessel jumped straight
out of white space right in front of us.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.800
-Valdack.
-That can't be.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.360
My data scan indicates
a heavily armored Gorgan Dreadnought,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.040
vessel ID number 9864321.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.360
Thank you, Dudani. Valdack must have
hijacked it from the Fermi hub

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.840
and tracked our position.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.040
-Tulaska, shield status?
-Shields 100%.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.320
-Helmsman Packer?
-Captain.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.400
-Prime rear thrusters.
-Rear thrusters primed.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.680
[Walton]
If that's Valdack, he'll rip us to shreds.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.640
Captain, we have to surrender.
There's no other way.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.760
Let's not lose our heads,
Lieutenant Walton.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:08.880
[zapping]

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.400
-Shields at 68%.
-[alarm wailing]

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.560
Heavy damage reported,
decks six through ten.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.280
Fires in med center
and major rupture to cargo bay Alpha.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.240
We've got no choice!

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.720
Do you want me to open comms
with Valdack's craft, Captain?

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.320
-Negative.
-[zapping]

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.080
[all groan]

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.800
-Shields at 54%.
-There's no way out.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.840
-Captain, please.
-[Daly] Not now, Walton.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.000
Helmsman Packer,
take us into that asteroid gas cluster.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.440
-Into the cluster?
-That's suicide, sir.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.960
It is our only chance.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.040
[Daly] That gas cluster is charged
with ionized pyron particles.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.480
If our shields hold, we can use them
to increase our photon intensity.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.320
Packer, increase thrusters.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.560
[engine thrusts]

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.240
[Tulaska] Shields at 43%.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.040
It'll tear the ship apart, Captain!

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.720
Walton, you are a Space Fleet officer.
Act accordingly.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.960
-Shields at 32%.
-Valdack's not following.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.520
Packer, turn us around.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.840
[engine rumbles]

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.120
-[Daly] Tulaska, charge photon bolts.
-Bolts charged, Captain.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.400
-Fire!
-[zapping]

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.280
His hull's breached, shields gone.
He's defenseless.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.280
-Lieutenant Lowry, open comms.
-He's already hailing us, Captain.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.600
-[Daly] On screen.
-[bleeps]

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.720
<i>Captain Daly, may you drown</i>
<i>in the venom of 900 Tragorian snakes!</i>

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.800
[Daly] You are defeated, Valdack.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.960
Return the plasmorthian crystal
and we'll cause you no more damage.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.600
<i>You must think me a fool, Captain!</i>

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.160
<i>I know the crystal's capabilities,</i>
<i>and I will die before I give it up!</i>

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.000
I gave you a chance, Valdack,
showed you mercy.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.720
-Reflect on that while you can.
-[yells]

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.360
-Close comms.
-[bleeps]

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.240
-Tulaska, destroy his ship.
-Yes, Captain.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.600
[bleeping]

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.560
[zaps]

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.280
-That was incredible, Captain.
-You saved our lives.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.480
[Walton] I'm so sorry
I lost it back there, Captain.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.720
Not for the first time, Walton.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.520
And I should know by now
never to doubt you.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.000
-[alarm beeps]
-[Walton] Please forgive me.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.960
At ease, Walton.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.680
Captain, sensors indicate
an escape pod ejected

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.640
from Valdack's ship before detonation.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.720
He's escaping with the crystal.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.840
You want me to plot
a pursuit course, Captain?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.360
No.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.720
We'll let him go... for now.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.400
-Great decision-making, Captain.
-Three cheers for Captain Daly.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.480
-Hip hip.
-[all] Hooray!

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.400
-Hip hip.
-[all] Hooray!

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.560
-Hip hip.
-[all] Hooray!

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.840
♪ <i>For he's a jolly good fellow</i>
<i>For he's a jolly good fellow ♪</i>

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:53.440
<i>♪ For he's a jolly good fellow ♪</i>

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.360
<i>♪ And so say all of us ♪</i>

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.640
God bless you, Captain. God bless you.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:06.280
[elevator beeps]

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.400
[automated voice]<i> Thirteenth floor.</i>

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.960
<i>-Welcome to Callister.</i>
-Oh.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.240
Excuse me.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.280
Excuse me.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.080
Hey.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.560
[negative beep]

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.200
[negative beep]

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.600
Uh... Elena, my pass doesn't work.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.680
You must renew on first of each month.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:44.560
Yeah, I know that,
but the first was on the weekend, so...

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.400
OK.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.640
-[beeps]
-[doors open]

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.720
Thank you.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.520
You're welcome.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.440
[automated voice]<i> Prepare to enter</i>

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.480
<i>the most immersive gaming experience</i>
<i>in years,</i>

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.880
Infinity,<i> from Callister Inc.</i>

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.200
-Morning, Mr. Daly.
-Helmsman Packer.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.280
Huh?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.200
Uh, I mean, Mr. Packer. Nate.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.240
[laughs]

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.400
OK.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.360
[Daly] Are you making coffees?

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.440
Yeah.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.840
Do you think maybe
you could make me one too?

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:26.440
[laughs] Sure, sure. Uh, what do you want?

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.720
Just vanilla latte. Skim milk.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.280
Yeah, good call. 'Cause...

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.720
[Packer clears throat]

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.840
[chattering]

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.960
[woman]
...those are very, very big numbers.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.920
We might just have to hold you to that.
Well, no, yes, of course. [laughs]

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.360
Sure. Yes.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.800
[crashing]

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.440
Oh, are you OK, man?

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:47.920
[sighs]

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.040
I guess you didn't see my gym bag.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.800
Here. Come on. [strains]

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.160
-I'm sorry, bud. [pats]
-OK.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.240
You left it... [groans]

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.480
[man] You're gonna do it for me
and make it good.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.400
You know you are a god to me at least.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.520
[laughing]

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:25.400
[knock on door]

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:29.880
Oh. The ladies' bathroom is that way.
The sign's kind of confusing.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:34.200
You're Robert Daly, right?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.200
-Right.
-Yeah, hi.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.280
I'm Nanette, Nanette Cole.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.360
Um...

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:45.360
I started here today,
coding on the update,

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:49.600
and I just wanted to, uh,
pass on my admiration

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.000
to the person
who actually designed <i>Infinity.</i>

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.520
The procedural algorithm is amazing.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.160
It's just some beautiful code.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.800
Thank you.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:05.920
That's actually the reason
that I wanted to work here.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:11.760
-You must be busy. I'm so sorry.
-No, no, it's fine.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.200
-Sorry. [laughs]
-No.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.240
-Well, just fangirling. Sorry. Um...
-[both laugh]

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.600
[Nanette gasps]

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.160
Ooh... vintage.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.840
-Yeah, it's<i> Space Fleet.</i>
-Wow.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.520
[Daly] It's a TV show. Before your time.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.840
Before my time, actually.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.720
But it was... visionary.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.480
Is this on, like, tape?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.040
Yeah, I've got the VHS, the DVD, Blu-ray.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.080
The whole thing. Seasons one to six.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.560
Netflix has it these days, but...

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.840
Aboard the spaceship <i>USS Callister.</i>

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.440
-OK, yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.160
So-- OK, so Callister is like the, uh--

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.360
Yeah, when we set up the company, um...

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.920
I suggested we call it Callister
as kind of a little tribute.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.720
Walton didn't really get the reference,
but he let me have that one.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.560
Mini-skirted damsels.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.120
[laughs]

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.880
A little cold for that in space.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:22.360
That is just what a Bargradian
sand warrior would say.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.640
[Nanette chuckles]

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.760
[Walton] Bob, Christmas is closing in
like a goddamn meteor.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.600
We've got customers all over our balls
waiting for the <i>Infinity</i> update.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:33.040
Tell me it's gonna be up and running
before the weekend.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.920
-Oh, I'll ask Kabir--
-You're CTO. Don't ask anybody anything.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.720
You should be telling people things
like I'm telling you right now.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.520
-I'll talk to him.
-Good.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.920
-I'm sorry.
-OK.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.160
-Hello.
-[Nanette] Hello.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.520
Sorry, I couldn't find a good moment to...

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.480
Oh, you must be new.
Uh... I'm James Walton. I run the company.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:53.280
-[Nanette] I--
-Well, we run the company, kind of.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.560
Bob here is the hardware,
and I am the shiny front end.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.760
-I'm Nanette Cole.
-[Walton] Which department?

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.440
-Engine architecture.
-And it's your first day?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.520
Uh...

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.000
-[stutters] Yeah.
-Have you had the tour?

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.400
-[keyboard clicking]
-No, I...

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.480
Please, allow me.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:12.880
[Nanette] OK.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.080
It was so nice to meet you. [laughs]

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.320
[Walton] Just a little bit.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.000
It's a different environment
I set up here.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.880
People call it a carefree environment.
I call it "care-full."

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.800
-[Nanette] Interesting.
-Not scary.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.600
[chattering continuing]

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:37.960
Dudani?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.080
Kabir?

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.800
Mm. Mr. Daly.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:46.880
Do you have the latest ETA
on the update patch?

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.160
It's just there's still
some runtime errors.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.920
Well, the thing is, we could have it ready
by end of play today,

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.200
but if we had time,
we could alter the trading mechanics,

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.600
tweak the critical hit system,
but of course, that'd add another week,

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.240
maybe ten days or so.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.320
Mr. Daly?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:10.960
-Yeah. Yeah, do all of that, thank you.
-I'll... OK, we're on it.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.280
[chattering, laughing]

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.200
[number pad bleeps]

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.680
[door whirs]

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.720
-[device bleeps]
-[whirring]

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.320
[device boots up]

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.280
[Walton] Welcome back, Captain.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.400
Have you located Valdack's position?

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.920
Not yet, but our sensors
are scanning every star system

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
between here and Valatros.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.480
So your answer is no?

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.240
Uh...

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:51.720
I'm afraid so, sir.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.600
[Walton gasps, groans]

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.160
[grunting]

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.760
You... are pathetic, Walton. What are you?

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.360
-[Walton gasping]
-What's that?

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.960
[inhales] Pathetic.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:11.880
[gasps]

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.120
[groans, panting]

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.480
[Daly] So Valdack's out there somewhere

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.640
and you village idiots
are asleep at the wheel.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.840
You're not just disgraceful,
you're disgusting, all of you.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:35.240
So can you do one thing?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.440
Can you find Valdack?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.960
I'm not asking. I'm telling you!
Understand?

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.600
-Hmm?
-Yes.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:49.640
-[Daly] Yes?
-Yes, Captain. Yeah.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.840
-[Daly] Yes.
-Aye, Captain.

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:53.600
[Daly] Huh?

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:00.080
Well, all right.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.480
Tulaska, check security protocols.
If they've expired, you're in trouble.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.280
-Yes, Captain.
-[bleeping]

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.800
Dudani, recheck those probe results.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:12.200
-No room for errors.
-Of course, Captain.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:14.040
-Helmsman Packer?
-Captain.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.680
Vanilla latte.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.040
-Skim milk.
-At once.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.480
[Daly] Walton.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:39.680
Exit game.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:40.760
[device whirs]

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:45.760
[device bleeps]

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.800
[keyboard clicking]

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.920
Hi, Nanette. You feel like
you have everything you need here?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:03.840
Mm-hmm.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.480
-All right. That's a nice sweater.
-Oh. Thank you.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.240
-[Walton] Cashmere?
-[chattering]

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:10.920
[knock on door]

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.160
Mr. Daly, got that new ETA
on the update patch.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.840
-New ETA?
-Yeah, it's all good.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:20.080
But now we're looking
at December 24th for rollout.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.000
We don't patch until Christmas Eve?

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.560
Well, yeah, I mean,
with the alterations you approved.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:32.800
OK, OK. Thank you.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:33.880
[Dudani] OK.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.520
[door closes]

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:37.920
[knock on door]

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.480
-Hi, Robert.
-Hi.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.480
Um, I was just gonna fix a coffee.
Do you want one?

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.480
-Sure.
-OK.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:52.280
Um... vanilla latte with skim milk.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.640
-[Nanette] Okey-dokes.
-OK.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.040
Absolutely.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.000
[laughs]

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.640
Mm-hmm.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.960
-Well, yes, they are great numbers.
-[machine whirs]

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.680
[laughs] OK. Mm-hmm.

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.080
-Ta-ta.
-[device beeps]

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.320
Total fucking shitwit.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:17.160
-Do you want coffee?
-Um, Brushed Suede. Thank you.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.560
So how are you settling in?
Are you settling in?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:25.040
Uh, yeah, yeah.
Everyone here is really friendly.

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:29.960
And um...
it is not like my last job, thank God.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:33.320
-Yeah?
-It was a toxic workplace, you know.

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:37.720
-My boss was a major-league bully and...
-[machine beeps]

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.480
-It's not like here, like with Mr...
-Walton.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.680
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah. He's a really good guy.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.400
He's a bit of a player.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:47.320
Chuck a sandwich across the room,
he'll fuck it before it hits the ground,

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.960
-but he's basically an all right bloke.
-[chuckles]

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:54.960
OK. [laughs] Well, there's uh...
two bosses here anyway, so I guess--

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.720
-Two how?
-Robert Daly.

00:15:58.360 --> 00:15:59.280
Oh!

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.600
I mean, well, yeah, technically. [scoffs]

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.480
Mr. Daly is actually
the whole reason that I'm here.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.440
-Really? Interesting.
-[Nanette] I mean...

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:11.120
Who wouldn't wanna work under
an incredible mind like that, you know?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.160
His coding is... [laughs] It's sublime.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.880
Do you have a thing for him?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:21.120
Daly? No, no. No. It's not like that.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.440
[stammers] It's purely...
It's professional.

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:25.320
I like his code.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.680
Ah. Fucking hell,
I was gonna say, you know,

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.440
don't be too nice to him
'cause he gets a bit starey.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.240
Mm.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:37.040
Wide berth, that's my advice. Wide berth.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.120
-OK.
-Yeah.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.520
Thank you.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.960
-There you go.
-Thank you.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.400
[exhales]

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.720
-[Lowry] Bye.
-No bye. I'm coming.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.360
[Lowry] No. Suck a dick, Karl.

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:20.840
[woman] Later, guys.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.600
[machine beeps]

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:30.560
[whirring]

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.120
[beeping]

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.600
[automated voice]<i> Welcome to Callister.</i>

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.600
[card beeps]

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.160
[Daly] Thank you.

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:51.720
You're welcome.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.480
[chattering]

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.520
[Walton] Goddamn it, Robert!

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.520
-Christmas Eve. Really?
-Uh...

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.360
Not OK.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.480
[door slams]

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.960
[keyboard clicking]

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:27.760
[typing]

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:36.440
[electronic whirring]

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:38.800
[gasps]

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.120
[whirring]

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:45.640
[gasps]

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.160
Oh.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.440
[breathing heavily]

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:25.120
Hello? [echoes]

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:44.600
[gasps]

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.280
-[distant chatter]
-[gasps]

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.440
[gasping]

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.960
Oh, boy. It looks like
there's a new girl in the office.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.680
What's your name, hon?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.000
[Walton] Come in. Let me fix you a drink.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:45.160
We have everything
from Bengarian phlegm shots to uh...

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:48.240
ooh, distilled root blood
from the Cangor quadrant.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:52.240
What's your poison? Some of this
actually is poison, so don't be shy.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:55.240
Am I dreaming?

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:58.840
Yeah, no, no, 'fraid not.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:01.280
-I remember dreaming.
-[Packer] Me too.

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:03.400
[Nanette] But where am I?

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.440
This is the <i>USS Callister,</i>
Space Fleet's finest,

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:09.960
exploring the furthest reaches
of the known universe and beyond.

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:14.080
We are its loyal space crew
and now, apparently, so are you. Cheers.

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:15.960
[slurps]

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.480
Your name? Babe, what's your name?

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:21.160
Nanette. We've met.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:25.160
Maybe, in the real world.
I wouldn't have no way of knowing.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:29.240
-What do you mean?
-You'd better sit down.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:31.800
No, I don't... I don't wanna sit down.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:34.440
I wanna know what's going on.

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.240
You're on board Robert Daly's ship.

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:39.280
Robert Daly, the CTO?

00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:42.280
Here he's Captain Daly,
our fearless leader.

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:45.160
[Lowry] Yeah, you're seriously
gonna need to sit the fuck down.

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:47.760
-Uh...
-Welcome. [chuckles]

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:53.400
You are um... Hey, hey.
You're the intern from work, right? Nate?

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.440
Packer. Nate Packer.

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:58.600
Wait. So I'm still
just the intern out there?

00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:00.480
Jesus.

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:02.680
You're um... You're... You're...

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:05.280
Dudani. Diagnostics.

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:08.360
-Welcome.
-Right.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:14.720
-You're the receptionist, right?
-Elena.

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:18.360
-Your skin is blue.
-[Tulaska] Weird blue alien skin, I know.

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:20.120
It's fucked up.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:22.400
Almost sort of racist.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:24.800
[groans]

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:29.840
[strains] OK. Walt, fix her something,
something she'll recognize. Vodka.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:32.280
-Hey. So what's it like out there now?
-What?

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:34.320
-What year is it?
-[Lowry] Don't do her head in.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:38.440
-[Packer] What?
-What year? I... [stutters] saw you today.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:41.400
Ooh. Did you see me? Did I look thin? Hmm?

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:43.360
Like, wheatgrass yogurt thin?

00:23:44.160 --> 00:23:46.040
Can we not pop her fucking mind?

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.960
Someone needs
to be straight with me right now.

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:52.360
OK. OK, listen.

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.240
This is <i>Infinity.</i>

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:59.920
That's what we're all inside.
That's where all of this exists.

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:02.400
<i>Infinity</i>, the game?

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:05.520
Daly's got his own modded version
of <i>Infinity,</i>

00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:07.600
reskinned to look like
his favorite TV show.

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:10.640
<i>-Space Thing? Space Thing?</i>
<i>-Space Fleet.</i>

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:13.360
-Hence the groovy decor.
-And this tasteful get-up.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:15.440
<i>Infinity.</i>

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:18.360
That's an online game,
like a multiplayer deal. This... [inhales]

00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:22.960
This is his development build,
sealed off so he can control it.

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:24.600
He keeps it offline

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:27.080
so the custom code he's written
can't be detected and deleted.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:31.040
Mm. Yes, it's a bubble universe,
ruled by an asshole god.

00:24:32.760 --> 00:24:33.640
He...

00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:37.880
put us in... in here?

00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:38.840
Mm-hmm.

00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:40.040
Drink your vodka.

00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:43.520
-How do we get out?
-No, really, drink it.

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:45.400
Drink it.

00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:51.680
-You can't leave.
-[chokes] What?

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:53.040
None of us can.

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:56.440
-Because you're not actually you.
-[Nanette] What?

00:24:57.120 --> 00:25:01.080
I know it's mental,
but you're a copy of you.

00:25:01.160 --> 00:25:02.600
-A digital clone.
-No.

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:05.640
No, I am... I'm me. I am me.

00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:07.360
-I'm me.
-[Walton] No, not the real you.

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:11.800
Daly's created an identical
digital version of you, of all of us.

00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:15.160
From your DNA.
He'll have harvested it somehow.

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:17.800
He told me he got mine
from the rim of a smoothie cup.

00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:19.840
He retrieved Packer's juices
from the bathroom.

00:25:19.920 --> 00:25:22.520
Man, you have got to let that go.
She does not need details.

00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:24.120
Basically he's got a gizmo--

00:25:24.200 --> 00:25:26.120
I theorize an advanced
biometric DNA virtual clone.

00:25:26.200 --> 00:25:28.120
He's got a fucking gizmo.
That's what I said.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:30.920
He fed your DNA in,
he put you inside his computer

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:33.280
and, bam, you pop up here like a Pop-Tart.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.600
Yeah, we've all been through it.

00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:39.840
He brings us in for different reasons,
shit we did in the office.

00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:41.680
I called him out for staring.

00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:44.720
I reset admin permissions
on a test build for 14 minutes.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.440
Insufficient smiling.

00:25:46.520 --> 00:25:49.640
-I brought him the wrong sandwich.
-OK, never mind the reasons.

00:25:49.720 --> 00:25:52.320
The point is that we're stuck
in Daly's playground,

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:54.120
and that's all you need to know.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:57.920
This is a dream. Yeah, it has to be.

00:25:58.520 --> 00:26:03.480
It's more like an eternal waking nightmare
from which there is no escape.

00:26:04.760 --> 00:26:08.160
-No, no. No, no, no. No, no, no.
-[Lowry] Oh, for fuck's sake,

00:26:08.240 --> 00:26:09.840
I'm trying to break her in gently.

00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:11.680
The quicker she gets it,
the easier it'll be.

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:13.160
[whirring]

00:26:13.240 --> 00:26:14.680
[Tulaska] Daddy's home.

00:26:15.200 --> 00:26:16.640
[Packer] He'll be here any moment.

00:26:17.520 --> 00:26:19.120
[Nanette] No. I'm gonna get out of here.

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:21.120
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
You gotta stay on the bridge.

00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:22.240
He controls everything.

00:26:22.320 --> 00:26:24.120
-He does shit to make us cooperate.
-Get off.

00:26:24.200 --> 00:26:27.040
-You have no idea. I'm trying to help.
-[Lowry] Just leave it.

00:26:27.120 --> 00:26:29.040
He's gonna fuck us up
if she doesn't play ball.

00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:32.240
Yes, well, she's gonna have to work it out
for herself, like we all did.

00:26:32.920 --> 00:26:34.120
[panting]

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:38.720
[spaceship whirring]

00:26:40.280 --> 00:26:41.160
[groans]

00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:44.960
-There's gotta be a way out. Come on.
-[beeps]

00:26:50.600 --> 00:26:52.280
[whimpers]

00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:54.960
[screaming]

00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:02.320
[whimpers]

00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:07.200
Lieutenant Cole, welcome aboard.

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:11.760
Crew, we have a new member of the team,
Science Officer Nanette Cole.

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:13.760
Please, take your post.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:18.120
I believe we've finally managed
to track Valdack to an uncharted planet.

00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:20.640
-No.
-Take your post. That is an order.

00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:23.400
I'm not doing this.

00:27:25.080 --> 00:27:27.560
The whole thing's much better
if you let yourself get into it.

00:27:27.640 --> 00:27:32.080
If you think that I'm playing along
with your<i> Space Force</i> bullshit...

00:27:32.160 --> 00:27:33.920
<i>-Space Fleet.</i>
-[Nanette] Whatever.

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.720
-You can think again.
-This is my ship.

00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:41.080
-I am your captain. An order is an order.
-Then go fuck yourself.

00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:43.480
Sir.

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:47.560
OK. So we're doing it this way.

00:27:49.400 --> 00:27:50.280
[scoffs]

00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:53.080
[mocking] Are you gonna throw a fireball?

00:27:56.720 --> 00:27:57.600
[snaps fingers]

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:01.120
[muffled gasps]

00:28:02.120 --> 00:28:03.280
[thuds]

00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:04.520
[muffled sounds]

00:28:04.600 --> 00:28:09.800
Oh, dear. You can't see.
You can't breathe.

00:28:09.880 --> 00:28:11.000
Unpleasant, isn't it?

00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:13.840
[muffled groaning]

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:15.120
Do you submit?

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:18.000
You won't die, you know.

00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:22.840
No one dies in here unless I want them to.

00:28:24.280 --> 00:28:28.160
I can keep you like this forever
if I feel like it.

00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:31.840
Forever gasping for breath
with a mouth that isn't there.

00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:34.760
Do you submit?

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:35.920
[muffled agreement]

00:28:37.720 --> 00:28:38.680
Good girl.

00:28:39.880 --> 00:28:42.560
[gasps, coughing]

00:28:44.600 --> 00:28:47.080
[breathes heavily]

00:28:47.160 --> 00:28:51.160
Lieutenant Cole, Valdack's hideout.
Triangulate the signal, please.

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:58.520
[Nanette pants]

00:29:02.960 --> 00:29:04.680
[sobs]

00:29:09.840 --> 00:29:12.560
[whispers]
It's any button. They're all the same.

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:14.800
[beeps]

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:16.000
[beeps]

00:29:16.080 --> 00:29:17.160
Well?

00:29:17.240 --> 00:29:21.080
[gasping] I'm getting a signal
from a class five planet.

00:29:21.160 --> 00:29:23.400
-Rannotch.
-[Lowry] Rannoch.

00:29:24.520 --> 00:29:26.400
[stutters, whispers] Rannoch B.

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:30.600
Excellent. Dudani,
prepare the transmat system.

00:29:30.680 --> 00:29:33.520
-Of course, Captain.
-Walton, Packer, Lowry, with me.

00:29:33.600 --> 00:29:35.920
We'll transport down to the planet,
reclaim the crystal

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:37.960
and bring Valdack to justice.

00:29:39.680 --> 00:29:42.880
Actually, Cole, you come too.

00:29:42.960 --> 00:29:44.600
Perfect opportunity for you to prove

00:29:44.680 --> 00:29:47.920
you're more than a recommendation
from Space Fleet. What do you say?

00:29:57.680 --> 00:30:00.160
-Mr. Dudani, transport.
-Aye aye, Captain.

00:30:07.400 --> 00:30:08.400
[all exhale]

00:30:08.480 --> 00:30:11.160
[Nanette gasps, groans]

00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:19.120
[Daly] Breathable atmosphere.

00:30:19.200 --> 00:30:21.200
[device whirs]

00:30:21.280 --> 00:30:23.760
Scanning for plasmorthian traces.

00:30:26.200 --> 00:30:28.160
Crystal's this way. Let's go.

00:30:28.240 --> 00:30:31.320
-Nate. Hey, Nate.
-Helmsman Packer, OK?

00:30:31.400 --> 00:30:34.440
Call me Helmsman Packer. He hates it
when we don't use our proper titles.

00:30:34.520 --> 00:30:36.560
OK. You got a gun, so let's take him out.

00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:39.320
-Then give it to me.
-OK, one, our guns don't even work.

00:30:39.400 --> 00:30:44.200
Only his does. And two, the motherfucker
is invincible, OK? Come on, let's go.

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.400
At least you've got a gun.

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:53.440
[device whirring]

00:30:55.400 --> 00:30:56.440
-Captain.
-[Daly] Shh.

00:30:56.520 --> 00:30:59.240
We meet again, Captain Daly!

00:30:59.320 --> 00:31:02.800
[cackles]

00:31:03.240 --> 00:31:04.680
-We're trapped.
-[gun whirs]

00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:06.960
Not advisable.

00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:10.480
My plasma grenade
will turn you into screaming soup.

00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:12.360
He's not going to kill us, Captain.

00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:15.800
He had the element of surprise.
He'd have done it when he had the chance.

00:31:15.880 --> 00:31:19.200
Haven't worked out how to use the crystal,
have you, Valdack?

00:31:19.280 --> 00:31:22.760
It's true, I require
your Space Fleet knowledge.

00:31:22.840 --> 00:31:25.640
But it's also true
that you're gonna give it to me!

00:31:25.720 --> 00:31:26.720
Don't be so sure.

00:31:26.800 --> 00:31:28.480
[laughs]

00:31:28.560 --> 00:31:30.560
-Jesus. I...
-Shh.

00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:33.800
Let's see how your resolve holds up

00:31:33.880 --> 00:31:39.320
once you're devoured one by one
by my Arachnajax!

00:31:39.400 --> 00:31:41.440
[roars]

00:31:41.520 --> 00:31:44.520
-Holy shit. Oh, my God.
-[Walton] We're all gonna die.

00:31:45.800 --> 00:31:48.040
[Arachnajax snarls, snorts]

00:31:53.760 --> 00:31:54.760
[roars]

00:31:56.360 --> 00:31:59.600
Killing us won't make us tell you
how the crystal works, Valdack.

00:32:00.080 --> 00:32:03.200
-We will never...
-[device rings]

00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:06.240
Hold on. I think my pizza's here.

00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:09.040
-[sighs]
-[device rings]

00:32:09.120 --> 00:32:10.120
Pause game.

00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:11.480
[powering down]

00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:14.400
[Nanette] What's happening?

00:32:14.480 --> 00:32:16.280
[Walton] You heard him.
He paused the game.

00:32:16.360 --> 00:32:19.400
'Cause he's got a pizza delivery...
out there.

00:32:19.480 --> 00:32:21.240
[Arachnajax pants]

00:32:21.320 --> 00:32:24.480
[doorbell ringing]

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:29.000
Hold on.

00:32:29.080 --> 00:32:32.560
[doorbell continues]

00:32:35.680 --> 00:32:37.160
[Arachnajax exhales]

00:32:40.040 --> 00:32:41.920
[Packer] Watch out. He'll be back soon.

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:45.280
Ah. That's good.
This launcher's heavy as shit.

00:32:47.280 --> 00:32:48.680
[Valdack] How you holding up?

00:32:48.760 --> 00:32:50.440
You know, we're existing.

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:52.840
How you doing, Gillian?

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:55.360
[Arachnajax grunts]

00:32:56.240 --> 00:32:57.520
Well, yeah.

00:32:59.560 --> 00:33:01.800
-[Walton] Well, you look great.
-Her name's Gillian.

00:33:01.880 --> 00:33:04.120
-[Walton] Did you lose weight?
-She was in marketing.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:07.320
Yeah, Daly turned her into... that

00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:09.880
because she wouldn't play along
when he cloned her into here.

00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:12.880
[Lowry] This universe is littered
with things like her,

00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:15.200
poor fuckers who stepped out of line.

00:33:17.720 --> 00:33:19.320
-Thank you.
-[man] Thanks.

00:33:26.120 --> 00:33:27.200
[device whirs]

00:33:27.280 --> 00:33:29.120
-[Walton] Here comes Captain Dick.
